    "body": "@annevk ok, my question of risk means allowing sub-origin (subdomain of `https://example.com`) in access-control-allow-origin rather than specify single origin (just `https://example.com`).\r\nand you mean there are reasonable to allow them, but notation of `https://*.example.com` is hard to standardize (parsing/matching model etc). but `samesite` has [done](https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-httpbis-cookie-same-site-00) them already, so it's possible to use them instead of `https://*.example.com` notation. is that right ?",
