    "updated_at": "2019-07-18T11:32:36Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I'd prefer syntax that avoids new parsing and model requirements. I have these extensions in mind, but they require some implementer interest (which I think we have) and people to do the work (of writing the text and tests):\r\n\r\n* `same-site` token. If A requests B, it's a match if B's host is [same site](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#host-same-site) with A's host and B's scheme is A's scheme.\r\n* registrable domain in addition to origin (e.g., `example.com`). If A requests B, it's a match if A's host's registrable domain is `example.com`.\r\n* Multiple values, we'd now split the header value on commas and compare each value when trying to determine a match.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
